From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:24:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Route refused drawer comments to the registered card
 owner

Problem: a Desktop drawer opened on a replica receives foreign_card and
shows worker-only instructions instead of posting the user's comment.
Why: addComment routes only legacy no-profile hubTaskRefs; qualified
profile/board writes correctly avoid that lossy courier but have no
foreign-owner recovery. The backend refuses before any write and names
created_on in its stable foreign_card refusal. Existing drawer tests cover
an already-correct owner but not an opening connection holding a replica.

Recover only that definite refusal, match this task ID, resolve the owner
through the existing registered hub connection mapping, and retry once
with the captured profile and board. Do not retry uncertain network errors,
loop on the same connection, use an ambient profile or queue a second write.
Unreachable owners get plain-language next steps; a failed owner attempt
asks the user to check comments before retrying because its result may be
uncertain. Structured decisions and their authorization are unchanged.

Proof: new public addComment regressions fail on main (2 failures / 18
passes); fixed tests plus retry-safety controls pass (28). All Kanban
Desktop tests, tsc with 4GiB heap, affected eslint and scripts/check pass.
The default 2GiB tsc heap exhausted memory; 4GiB completed successfully.
Historical MacBook request route remains inferred, not directly recovered.
